WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.156 --> 00:00:02.849
(epic orchestral music)

00:00:02.849 --> 00:00:04.549
- [Narrator] In London,
Ontario, there lives a man

00:00:04.549 --> 00:00:07.453
whose basement is unlike
anything you've ever seen.

00:00:07.453 --> 00:00:08.806
This is Robert Wardhaugh.

00:00:08.806 --> 00:00:10.608
- Hi, my name is Robert Wardhaugh.

00:00:10.608 --> 00:00:12.142
- [Narrator] Robert has
been playing the same

00:00:12.142 --> 00:00:15.148
Dungeons and Dragons
campaign for over 30 years.

00:00:15.148 --> 00:00:16.535
- 35 years to be exact.

00:00:16.535 --> 00:00:17.392
- [Narrator] I'm sorry.

00:00:17.392 --> 00:00:18.559
- That's okay.

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:30.519
Welcome, would you like
to play a Dwarven rogue.

00:00:30.519 --> 00:00:32.371
You look like a rogue.

00:00:32.371 --> 00:00:34.330
- [Narrator] Wait, let's
back up for a second.

00:00:34.330 --> 00:00:36.806
Dungeons and Dragons is a
fantasy roleplaying game

00:00:36.806 --> 00:00:38.804
where a group of people
come together and play out

00:00:38.804 --> 00:00:41.347
adventures dictated by a dungeon master.

00:00:41.347 --> 00:00:43.686
These adventures, also
known as campaigns, are set

00:00:43.686 --> 00:00:45.447
in the Dungeons and Dragons world

00:00:45.447 --> 00:00:46.936
and normally have an end point.

00:00:46.936 --> 00:00:49.983
Or they just fizzle out due to
people's lack of commitment.

00:00:49.983 --> 00:00:51.522
But Robert is in a league of his own

00:00:51.522 --> 00:00:53.235
and here's why:

00:00:53.235 --> 00:00:55.705
The dude has a serious collection.

00:00:55.705 --> 00:00:59.541
- I think our collection of
miniatures is around 20,000

00:00:59.541 --> 00:01:02.731
and then over the years
I discovered terrain.

00:01:02.731 --> 00:01:05.376
Ultimately, I'm a collector
also and a lot of my enjoyment

00:01:05.376 --> 00:01:08.940
comes from being able to get
new stuff and to put new stuff

00:01:08.940 --> 00:01:10.793
on the table so the players

00:01:10.793 --> 00:01:14.251
are constantly coming across new settings.

00:01:14.251 --> 00:01:17.585
Because it's a game that
doesn't stick to one particular

00:01:17.585 --> 00:01:20.424
campaign setting, I'm able to use any figs

00:01:20.424 --> 00:01:23.100
that actually fit the world.

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:27.035
And so it is a long
process but over 35 years,

00:01:27.035 --> 00:01:29.047
you could develop quite the collection.

00:01:29.047 --> 00:01:30.116
- [Narrator] As Robert's collection grew,

00:01:30.116 --> 00:01:31.523
so did the number of players.

00:01:31.523 --> 00:01:34.515
Word began to spread about
the never-ending campaign.

00:01:34.515 --> 00:01:37.062
- We have people coming from
all over the country to play,

00:01:37.062 --> 00:01:38.367
often flying in.

00:01:38.367 --> 00:01:39.997
- [Narrator] Wait, all over the country?

00:01:39.997 --> 00:01:41.011
- That's right.

00:01:41.011 --> 00:01:43.582
- [Player] Robert, can we play now?

00:01:43.582 --> 00:01:44.516
- [Narrator] These are some of the people

00:01:44.516 --> 00:01:46.152
who play in Robert's game.

00:01:46.152 --> 00:01:47.857
Where are you guys from?

00:01:47.857 --> 00:01:50.028
- I flew in from Saskatoon, Saskatchewan.

00:01:50.028 --> 00:01:51.618
- I drove in from Toronto.

00:01:51.618 --> 00:01:52.451
- Brussels, Ontario.

00:01:52.451 --> 00:01:53.284
- Komoka, Ontario.

00:01:53.284 --> 00:01:54.423
- Calgary, Alberta.

00:01:54.423 --> 00:01:56.932
- [Narrator] Hold on, what
happens if people can't fly in

00:01:56.932 --> 00:01:59.889
or drive to Robert's house to play?

00:01:59.889 --> 00:02:00.999
- Hey everyone.

00:02:00.999 --> 00:02:03.332
- [Narrator] Problem solved.

00:02:04.517 --> 00:02:08.248
- On top of the ridge,
looking down upon this and.

00:02:08.248 --> 00:02:10.068
The game has always been determined,

00:02:10.068 --> 00:02:11.835
really through a friendship.

00:02:11.835 --> 00:02:16.140
It's really been a way that
I keep my friends together.

00:02:16.140 --> 00:02:19.850
I knew early on that if I
was able to create a game

00:02:19.850 --> 00:02:22.006
that was good enough, and
that means it had to be better

00:02:22.006 --> 00:02:24.462
than video games, it had to
be better than any other game

00:02:24.462 --> 00:02:25.908
that they could find, that
they would keep coming,

00:02:25.908 --> 00:02:30.128
no matter where I was and so
that takes again, imagination

00:02:30.128 --> 00:02:32.703
and it takes change and
it takes having a system

00:02:32.703 --> 00:02:35.687
that is constantly
dynamic, that is changing,

00:02:35.687 --> 00:02:38.511
that is growing and that is
constantly getting better.

00:02:38.511 --> 00:02:42.178
(dramatic orchestral music)

